    "result_text": "All tests pass. The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `birthDate` \u2192 `ageBand` derivation on the `POST /api/owners` / `GET /api/owners/{id}` endpoint.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** (drives DTO generation):\n   - Added optional `birthDate` (ISO `date`) to `OwnerFields` \u2014 the request-settable fields.\n   - Added read-only `ageBand` (string) to the `Owner` response schema, documented as `MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`, absent when no birth date is supplied.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `birthDate` `LocalDate` field (mapped to a `birth_date` column) with getter/setter.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `formatAgeBand` method and wired it into `toOwnerDto` via `@Mapping(... qualifiedByName)`. It computes `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()` and returns `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), or `SENIOR` (\u226565); returns `null` (field absent) when `birthDate` or `registrationDate` is missing. `birthDate` itself maps through `toOwner`/`toOwnerDto` automatically by name.\n\n4. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 added the `birth_date DATE` column to the `owners` table.\n\nThe age band is computed against `registrationDate` as specified. For the acceptance test (`birthDate=1990-01-01`, registrationDate defaulting to today), age 36 \u2192 `ADULT`, which the test asserts.\n\nNote: the code follows the project's existing pattern for derived read-only fields (`contactPreference`, `locality`), keeping `ageBand` a plain string rather than a generated enum to stay consistent and avoid referencing a nested generated type in the MapStruct interface.",
