    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots into the existing pattern exactly:\n\n- `formatAgeBand` is placed alongside the sibling derived-field helpers (`formatContactPreference`, `formatMembershipLevel`, `formatLocality`, etc.) in `OwnerMapper`, which is where this codebase already computes read-only DTO fields. It uses the same `@Named` + `qualifiedByName` wiring, the same null-guard shape, and the same Javadoc structure (including the standard `@Named` note). No new catch-all is introduced \u2014 the mapper was already the home for exactly this kind of derivation.\n- The `birthDate` field, getter, and setter on `Owner` mirror the adjacent `registrationDate` member, and the `@Column` mapping is consistent.\n- The schema change is applied uniformly across all four dialects (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) in the same column position, so no dialect is left inconsistent.\n- The OpenAPI additions correctly model `birthDate` as a writable request field and `ageBand` as a `readOnly` derived field, with descriptions consistent with the neighboring derived fields.\n\nNothing is duplicated and the logic lives in the natural unit. A maintainer of this repo would find this a routine, idiomatic addition.",
